        longDescription: "Nailary is a web application in production that helps nail technicians and other independent professionals manage their appointments. Each professional creates an account, sets up services and business hours, and shares a booking link where clients choose one or more services, a day, and a time without signing up; the confirmation arrives by email. From the dashboard, professionals manage their calendar by day, week, or month, add appointments requested through WhatsApp or in person, check client records, and set time off, minimum notice, and time between appointments. I built the frontend with React and TypeScript, and an API with Node.js and Express on PostgreSQL, using SQL queries and versioned migrations, without an ORM. The main challenge was availability: each service can have options that change its price and duration, and time slots are calculated from the full appointment, breaks, time off, and existing bookings. To keep two simultaneous bookings from taking the same slot, availability is checked again inside a transaction with PostgreSQL locks, and idempotency keys prevent duplicate submissions. I also implemented custom authentication with signed sessions and scrypt password hashing, bot protection with Cloudflare Turnstile and rate limits, emails with Resend, image storage on Cloudflare R2, a prerendered landing page for SEO, and support for installing it as a PWA. It includes unit tests and integration tests against a real PostgreSQL database.",
